    "findings": [
      "Directly read all 54 encoded source samples on all 14 boards. Upscaling prerequisite shows 32 gray projected cells against 8 teal cells, then restores the 32-cell output; half width times half height means quarter pixel count, not four times whole-frame FPS. The initial title/label-only stage is intentional.",
      "Mobile local-memory prerequisite separates a short teal material-to-lighting path from an orange external store/reload branch beneath the projected tile. Forward/Deferred calculation order and tile-local memory location remain distinct; no measured bandwidth number is invented.",
      "Path probability prerequisite uses values 2 and 8, each target probability 0.5, mean 5, with selection probabilities 0.2 and 0.8. Both explicitly corrected contributions equal 5 in this special example; the diagram does not claim perfect reconstruction for general distributions.",
      "Path survival prerequisite shows probability 0.8 with surviving weight 1.25 and probability 0.2 with contribution zero. The displayed expectation 0.8 times 1.25 plus 0.2 times zero equals 1; termination is probabilistic and does not mean exactly every fifth path. The variance caveat remains visible.",
      "Source boundaries at frames 908, 1912 and 3194 switch completely to the new scene; final frame 4230 remains populated and readable. Black background, white text, restrained teal/orange emphasis and projected faces are present in these source samples. Continuous-motion and final burned captions require separate review."
    ],
